# Copy this file to .env (in this same repo-root directory) and fill in
# the values you need for your machine. .env is loaded automatically at
# startup — see docs/configuration.md for what each variable does and
# what the sidecar does when it's left unset.
#
# .env is gitignored: it's machine-specific, never commit your real one.
# A real environment variable (a shell `export`/`$env:`, or one baked into
# a launcher) always wins over a value in here — this file is a
# convenience for a checkout, never an override of something you
# deliberately set elsewhere.
#
# Do not wrap values in quotes, even if the path has spaces in it — quotes
# are not needed either way, and a double-quoted value undergoes escape
# processing ("\n" becomes an actual newline, "\t" a tab, and so on) which
# can silently corrupt a Windows path containing one of those letters
# right after a backslash (C:\Users\nick\... is fine unquoted; the exact
# same path double-quoted turns "\n" into a line break). Prefer forward
# slashes for paths on every OS, including Windows (C:/Users/you/...) —
# this project's own code follows the same convention, and it sidesteps
# the whole backslash question.

# Where your Seestar photo archive lives on disk (the directory holding
# one <target>/ + <target>-sub/ pair per imaged target). Unset: the
# sidecar still boots and serves the store's own data; /api/projects_combined's
# archive_status field reports {"configured": false, ...}.
# SEESTAR_ARCHIVE_DIR=C:/Users/you/OneDrive/Documents/SeeStar

# Path to your seestar-mcp checkout — the sidecar spawns it as a stdio
# subprocess. Unset: the sidecar still boots, but every tool-backed route
# 502s with a message naming this variable until it's set (or you run
# with SEESTAR_REPLAY=1 below instead).
# SEESTAR_AI_DIR=C:/Users/you/seestar-mcp

# The Seestar's OWN SMB share on the LAN (e.g. \\Seestar\... or
# \\seestar.local\...) — a DIFFERENT path from SEESTAR_ARCHIVE_DIR above,
# which is a periodic export, not live. The Live session screen's preview
# card reads a live stacked/per-sub thumbnail from here, only while a
# session is confirmed running. Needs AllowInsecureGuestAuth enabled on this
# machine for most Seestar shares (a host-wide relaxation, not something
# this repo enables for you) — see docs/configuration.md before setting
# this. Unset: the preview card reports {"reason": "not_configured"}.
# SEESTAR_LIVE_SHARE_DIR=//Seestar/EMMC Images

# Path to SeeStar-AI's provenance.jsonl (the operator panel's read-only
# activity feed tails this). Unset: defaults to
# <SEESTAR_AI_DIR>/data/provenance.jsonl when SEESTAR_AI_DIR is set, else
# "not configured". Only set this if your checkout's data/ directory is
# somewhere else.
# SEESTAR_PROVENANCE_PATH=C:/Users/you/seestar-mcp/data/provenance.jsonl

# Where fetched sky-survey cutouts are cached. Unset: defaults to
# sidecar/.cache/target_images, already portable — only set this if you
# want the cache to live somewhere else.
# SEESTAR_IMAGE_CACHE_DIR=C:/Users/you/AppData/Local/seestar-dashboard/images

# Where completed Review & QA analyses are cached, one JSON per target.
# Unset: defaults to sidecar/.cache/qa_analysis, already portable and
# already gitignored — only set this if you want the cache elsewhere.
# Deleting it costs nothing but recomputing, which takes minutes a target.
# SEESTAR_QA_CACHE_DIR=C:/Users/you/AppData/Local/seestar-dashboard/qa

# What this process calls itself in seestar-mcp's shared provenance log.
# The one variable here the sidecar SETS rather than reads: it passes it
# down to the seestar_mcp.server subprocess, defaulting to "console" so
# the dashboard's own calls are distinguishable from the agent's. Your
# value wins if you set one. Only worth setting if you run two consoles
# against one server. No effect under SEESTAR_REPLAY=1 (no subprocess).
# SEESTAR_CLIENT_ID=console-shed

# Port the dashboard serves on. Unset: defaults to 8787.
# SEESTAR_PORT=8080

# Extra host names the console may be reached by, comma-separated, no ports.
# Requests with any other Host header are refused (DNS-rebinding defence).
# Only needed with --host beyond loopback. The API has NO authentication:
# see docs/configuration.md "Network exposure" before exposing it.
# SEESTAR_ALLOWED_HOSTS=console.lan

# Set to 1 to serve recorded fixtures (fixtures/*.json) instead of
# spawning a live seestar-mcp server — no telescope, no SEESTAR_AI_DIR,
# no network needed.
# SEESTAR_REPLAY=1
